# What NOT to ship to Elastic Beanstalk.
#
# **This file replaces .gitignore for bundling.** The moment .ebignore exists, the EB CLI stops consulting
# .gitignore entirely — so every rule that protected a secret has to be restated here. That is the whole
# reason this file leads with the credentials: the AWS keys live in backend/.env.local, they are ignored by
# git, and without the line below they would be ignored by git and *shipped to AWS in the bundle*.
#
# On EB the credentials come from environment properties instead (S3_BUCKET, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID,
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_REGION), which is why the file is not needed in the bundle at all.
.env.local
.env.local.backup

# Nothing to install: this package has no runtime dependencies.
node_modules

# The seeds and ingests author documents from a demo package that is not deployed. They are development
# tools; the server reads the finished documents out of S3.
scripts/

# Local scratch
*.log
*.tmp
db.json.tmp
